<body lang=3D"ZH-CN" link=3D"#0563C1" vlink=3D"#954F72" style=3D"text-justi=
fy-trim:punctuation">
<div class=3D"WordSection1">
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"color:#1F497D">Hi,<o:p=
></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"color:#1F497D">&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; We met a problem on ubuntu17.10 for arm serve=
r with amdgpu(AMD RADEON PRO WX7100),&nbsp; we use open source driver which=
 are integrated in ubuntu17.10. And the architecture is AArch64-linux-gnu.<=
o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"color:#1F497D">&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; we install :<o:p></o:p></span></p=
>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"color:#1F497D">&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; apt-get i=
nstall xserver-xorg xinit xfce4 and mesa-utils glmark2<o:p></o:p></span></p=
>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"color:#1F497D">&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; we start x server :<o:p></o:p></s=
pan></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"color:#1F497D">&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; sta=
rtx<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US" style=3D"color:#1F497D">&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; and then the monitor shows the sc=
reen and the screen is blurred( something wrong).<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><img width=3D"685" height=3D"51=
4" id=3D"=CD=BC=C6=AC_x0020_1" src=3D"cid:image001.jpg-20mpeJEqQGmVUEZnpbf10DRmByFHzeGd@public.gmane.org" a=
lt=3D"cid:image001.jpg-Y1ha6cqgvy7Foe5DTwV5pTRmByFHzeGd@public.gmane.org"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; And I have tried some opengl applications, the output has=
 same problem.(something is missing or &nbsp;in the wrong place.)<o:p></o:p=
></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; But in a x86_64 architecture server, with same OS. The sc=
reen output is normal. (I check xorg\DDX\mesa\libdrm etc.all the versions a=
re the same with aarch64 server.)<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">What I have done:<o:p></o:p></s=
pan></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 1</span><span style=3D"font-family:=CB=CE=CC=E5">=A1=A2</=
span><span lang=3D"EN-US">I upgrade kernel to 4.15-rc2 ,upgrade DRM to 3.23=
,upgrade DDX to 1.40,upgrade mesa to 17.2.6, but the problem still exist.<o=
:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 2</span><span style=3D"font-family:=CB=CE=CC=E5">=A1=A2</=
span><span lang=3D"EN-US">I enable =A1=AEshadowprimary=A1=AF option,<b> the=
 screen output became normal</b>, but the<b> performance drop quickly</b>=
=A1=AA=A1=AAglxgears drop from 4800fps to
 600fps, glmark drop from 4300 score to 730 score. <o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; <o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; I doubt there are something different in aarch64 and x86_=
64 but I don=A1=AFt know.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Any Advice or trial&nbsp; suggestion are welcome.<o:p></o=
:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&=
nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; Thanks.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US">Rejohn.<o:p></o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
<p class=3D"MsoNormal"><span lang=3D"EN-US"><o:p>&nbsp;</o:p></span></p>
